    <briefdescription>
<para>Complete downsampling policy for a single metric. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Declares the ordered list of resolution tiers from finest to coarsest. The pipeline computes aggregates in that order: tier[0] reads raw data, tier[1] reads tier[0] output, etc.</para>
<para>Example – typical sensor/metrics pipeline: <programlisting><codeline><highlight class="normal">DownsamplingPolicy<sp/>p<sp/>=<sp/><ref refid="structthemis_1_1_downsampling_policy_1a245d034210cefa55796ba035658d31a0" kindref="member">DownsamplingPolicy::defaultPolicy</ref>(</highlight><highlight class="stringliteral">&quot;cpu_usage&quot;</highlight><highlight class="normal">);</highlight></codeline>
<codeline><highlight class="normal"></highlight><highlight class="comment">//<sp/>Tiers:<sp/>1m<sp/>(7d),<sp/>1h<sp/>(90d),<sp/>1d<sp/>(2y)</highlight></codeline>
</programlisting> </para>
    </detaileddescription>
